<title>PORTUGAL: World Jan-Feb copper consumption rises on year-ago.</title>
<headline>World Jan-Feb copper consumption rises on year-ago.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>World copper consumption for the combined months of January and February 1997 was 7.5 percent higher than for the first two months of 1996, the International Copper Study Group (ICSG) said.</p>
<p>World refined copper consumption and supply trends, 1996-97</p>
<p>		 Thousand tonnes, copper</p>
<p>						  Jan-Feb 96    Jan-Feb 97</p>
<p>World consumption			   1,950	     2,095</p>
<p>World mine capacity			 2,034	     2,054</p>
<p>World mine production		     1,693	     1,858</p>
<p>Percent capacity utilisation		 83.2		90.5</p>
<p>Primary refined production		1,691	     1,799</p>
<p>Secondary refined production		310		 332</p>
<p>Refined production			  2,001	     2,130</p>
<p>(secondary and primary)</p>
<p>Percent scrap in total			 15.5		15.6</p>
<p>refined production</p>
<p>Refined stocks (end of period)	    709		  563</p>
<p>Four weeks of world consumption	   910		  994</p>
<p>Period stock change			    23		   85</p>
<p>Refined surplus/deficit			52		   35</p>
<p>Source: ICSG, May 1997</p>
<p>--Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
